    <dashboard name='Supplier Performance Overview' type='storyboard'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/CategoryInsightsReports/SupplierPerformanceOverview?rev=' id='SupplierPerformanceOverview' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/CategoryInsightsReports' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='964' maxwidth='2016' minheight='964' minwidth='2016' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98340' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99206' x='397' y='830'>
            <zone h='5187' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99206' x='397' y='830' />
            <zone h='10477' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99206' x='397' y='6017' />
            <zone h='82676' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99206' x='397' y='16494'>
              <flipboard active-id='5' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='Usage Instructions' captured-sheet='Supplier Performance Overview Instructions' id='2'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <dashboard name='Supplier Performance Overview Instructions'>
                        <zone id='5'>
                          <formatted-text>
                            <run fontsize='15'>1. The dashboard is split in 4 separate sheets by Region. Navigate to the region you are interested in. </run>
                            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>2. Limit the </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>Date Range</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'> for faster loading times. Make sure to include both your current period and previous period in the range of the </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>&quot;Date&quot; Filter. </run>
                            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>i.e if you want to compare April to March, make sure that both months are selected in the &quot;Date&quot; Range Filter.</run>
                            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>3. Select you </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>CP (Current Period)</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>  and </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>PP (Previous Period)</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>Æ </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>Start</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'> and </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>End</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>Æ </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>dates</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>. Important to remember here is that the </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e15759' fontsize='15'>lowest level of granularity is Week. </run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>This means if you select only 3 days from a week, Tableau will take the full week, regardless. </run>
                            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>4. You can also filter the dashboard for particular categories, subcategories, warehouses. </run>
                            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>5. You can expand to </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>Product</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'> view by clicking the </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>&quot;+&quot; </run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>on top of column </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>&quot;Brand&quot;. </run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>To aggregate only by supplier, click the </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>&quot;-&quot;</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'> on top of  column </run>
                            <run bold='true' fontsize='15'>&quot;Supplier&quot;</run>
                            <run fontsize='15'>.</run>
                          </formatted-text>
                        </zone>
                      </dashboard>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='APAC' captured-sheet='Supplier Overview APAC' id='3'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Supplier/ Brand APAC'>
                        <filter class='quantitative' column='[federated.0ml98eq0rv4v8i1ckkalg0pshoxb].[none:Calculation_5269704190573768709:qk]' included-values='all' />
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Europe' captured-sheet='Supplier Overview Europe' id='1'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Supplier/ Brand Europe'>
                        <filter class='quantitative' column='[federated.02hl0g90g3xvuy1h99jr40wfqlzu (copy)].[none:Calculation_5269704190573768709:qk]' included-values='all' />
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='LATAM' captured-sheet='Supplier Overview LATAM' id='4'>
